"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". This article rounds up the three pieces ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The offline-aware variant","anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" indicating no network connectivity (","type":"text"},{"code":".notConnectedToInternet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".networkConnectionLost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or a timed-out request (","type":"text"},{"code":".timedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). When it’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a ","type":"text"},{"code":"wifi.exclamationmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other error, including other ","type":"text"}